module bankr-ohs-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frbp9006.{ frbp9006 }
import frbp.events.{ FirstMeetingDate, OrderForReliefEntered, PetitionFiled }

// The Bankr. S.D. Ohio court's own periods and page limit, counted under
// FRBP 9006(a), the FRCP 6(a) method: the Local Bankruptcy Rules with
// amendments effective October 1, 2020. General Orders 50-1 (LBR
// 2016-1(b)(2)(A), the chapter 13 no-look fee, cases filed on or after
// February 24, 2021) and 59-1 (LBR 5081-1(b), manner of fee payment, July
// 5, 2023) are vendored layers but change no period, so no period takes a
// dated version. The FRBP periods (schedules, claims, the chapter 13 plan,
// discharge, dischargeability, exemptions, the adversary answer, appeals)
// are lit/frbp's and are not declared again, nor are the national periods
// the rules repeat: the 21-day notice of a home-equity payment change (LBR
// 3001-2, FRBP 3002.1(b)) and the 30-day § 523(a)(6) period after a
// hardship discharge (LBR 4007-1(b), FRBP 4007(d)). Stated in the rules but
// not declared: the business-day and working-day periods (the ballot
// certification three business days before confirmation, LBR 3018-2;
// perfection documents seven business days after a cash collateral motion,
// 4001-2; closing statements one working day before and proceeds three
// working days after a sale, 6004-1); the later-of period to object to an
// amended chapter 13 plan (the later of 21 days after service and 14 days
// after the § 341 meeting concludes, 3015-2(a), 3015-3(a)); the court's own
// acts (the 30-day final decree notice a year after confirmation,
// 3022-1(a); the clerk's transmittal seven days after withdrawal briefing
// closes, 5011-1(d)); the cash collateral investigation windows of 75 and
// 60 days, conditions on a financing order's terms (4001-2); the five days
// after the petition within which a § 362(c)(3) or (c)(4) motion needs no
// expedited hearing (4001-1(b)), and the seven days before the § 341
// meeting before which an abandonment request may not be made (6007-1(c)),
// bounds on when a paper may be filed rather than deadlines; and immediate
// duties (notice of postpetition property, 4002-1(c)).
/// A brief or memorandum, except upon leave of court for good cause shown
/// (LBR 9013-2(a)).
limit brief { pages <= 20 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 9013-2(a)" } cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 9013-2(a)"

/// A petition is filed without photo identification of the debtors (LBR
/// 1002-1).
event PetitionWithoutIdFiled()
/// An order reopening a closed case so the debtor may amend the schedules
/// to add a prepetition creditor is entered (LBR 1009-1(b)).
event ReopeningOrderEntered()
/// The chapter 7 trustee serves the Summary of the Trustee's Final Report
/// and Applications for Compensation (LBR 2002-1(d)).
event FinalReportSummaryServed()
/// A motion to reschedule a § 341 meeting is served, as shown on its
/// certificate of service (LBR 2003-1(b)).
event RescheduleMotionServed()
/// An order dismissing a chapter 13 case before confirmation is entered
/// (LBR 2016-1(b)(5)).
event Chapter13DismissalEntered()
/// The debtor's attorney's legal representation in a chapter 13 case is
/// discontinued (LBR 2016-1(b)(6)).
event RepresentationDiscontinued()
/// An official committee holds its first meeting (LBR 2071-1).
event CommitteeFirstMeeting()
/// A judge's order requiring an attorney to show cause why the attorney
/// should not be disciplined is served (LBR 2090-2).
event ShowCauseOrderServed()
/// The chief district judge's interim disciplinary order is entered by the
/// clerk of the district court (LBR 2090-2(d)(4)).
event InterimDisciplineOrderEntered()
/// A trial or hearing on any matter is scheduled to be held (LBR
/// 2091-1(c)).
event TrialOrHearingScheduled()
/// An objection to a claim is served, as shown on its certificate of
/// service (LBR 3007-1).
event ClaimObjectionServed()
/// The § 341 meeting of creditors is concluded (LBR 3012-1, 3015-3(a)).
event MeetingConcluded()
/// A motion to modify a confirmed chapter 13 plan is served (LBR
/// 3015-2(c)).
event PlanModificationMotionServed()
/// An order granting a chapter 11 enlargement of time is served (LBR
/// 3016-1(b)).
event ExclusivityEnlargementServed()
/// The chapter 11 confirmation hearing is scheduled to be held (LBR
/// 3020-1).
event ConfirmationHearingScheduled()
/// The order setting the final hearing on a motion for relief from stay is
/// entered, or the motion is served (LBR 4001-1(a)(8)).
event StayHearingOrderEntered()
/// The chapter 13 trustee files the Certification of Final Payment (LBR
/// 4002-1(d)).
event FinalPaymentCertified()
/// The trustee serves a written request on the debtor for information or
/// documents (LBR 4002-1(f)).
event TrusteeRequestServed()
/// A motion for withdrawal of the reference is served, as shown on its
/// certificate of service (LBR 5011-1(b)).
event WithdrawalMotionServed()
/// A response to a motion for withdrawal of the reference is served (LBR
/// 5011-1(c)).
event WithdrawalResponseServed()
/// A notice of a proposed use, sale or lease of estate property is served
/// (LBR 6004-1(a)).
event SaleNoticeServed()
/// A sale of property not in the ordinary course of business is completed
/// (LBR 6004-1(a)(2)).
event SaleCompleted()
/// A notice of abandonment is served (LBR 6007-1(a)).
event AbandonmentNoticeServed()
/// The trustee receives a party's written request for abandonment (LBR
/// 6007-1(c)).
event AbandonmentRequestReceived()
/// The Order Governing Pretrial and Trial Procedures is entered (LBR
/// 7016-1(a)).
event PretrialOrderEntered()
/// A motion for a protective order or to compel discovery is filed (LBR
/// 7026-1).
event DiscoveryMotionFiled()
/// A memorandum in opposition to a discovery motion is filed (LBR 7026-1).
event DiscoveryOppositionFiled()
/// An individual appearing pro se changes mailing address or telephone
/// number (LBR 9011-2(a)).
event ProSeAddressChanged()
/// A motion or application is served, as shown on its certificate of
/// service (LBR 9013-1(b)).
event MotionServed()
/// A response memorandum to a motion or application is served (LBR
/// 9013-1(c)).
event ResponseServed()
/// A hearing at which the standing trustee's financial records are offered
/// is scheduled to be held (LBR 9070-1).
event TrusteeRecordsHearingScheduled()
/// The time to respond to a motion or application expires with no response
/// (LBR 9072-1(e)).
event ResponseTimeExpired()
/// A hearing or trial is held (LBR 9072-1(f)).
event HearingOrTrialHeld()
/// The court is informed of the parties' resolution of a matter before a
/// hearing or trial (LBR 9072-1(g)).
event ResolutionReported()
/// A brief or memorandum is filed (LBR 9013-2(a)).
event BriefFiled() paper brief

/// LBR 1002-1: if a petition is filed without photo identification, a copy
/// is provided to the Clerk's Office for every debtor named, or a motion
/// for waiver is made, within 14 days.
deadline photo-id-period: 14.days after PetitionWithoutIdFiled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 1002-1"

/// LBR 1007-2(a): unless otherwise ordered, in an involuntary case the
/// debtor files the mailing list of creditors and parties in interest not
/// later than 7 days after entry of the order for relief.
deadline involuntary-mailing-list-period: 7.days after OrderForReliefEntered() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 1007-2(a)"

/// LBR 1009-1(b): after a closed case is reopened to add a prepetition
/// creditor, the amendment is filed within 14 days of the entry date of the
/// reopening order.
deadline reopened-amendment-period: 14.days after ReopeningOrderEntered() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 1009-1(b)"

/// LBR 1074-1(d): no later than 14 days after a voluntary petition (or the
/// order for relief in an involuntary case), the individual responsible for
/// an entity debtor is identified by name and title in a paper filed with
/// the clerk.
deadline responsible-person-period: 14.days after PetitionFiled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 1074-1(d)"

/// LBR 2002-1(d): the chapter 7 trustee serves the summary of the final
/// report and fee applications with the thirty-day Notice of Deadline to
/// Object.
deadline final-report-objection-period: 30.days after FinalReportSummaryServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 2002-1(d)"

/// LBR 2003-1(b): a response to a motion to reschedule a § 341 meeting is
/// filed within 7 days from the date of service on the certificate of
/// service.
deadline reschedule-response-period: 7.days after RescheduleMotionServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 2003-1(b)"

/// LBR 2016-1(b)(5): the fee application of the debtor’s attorney in a
/// chapter 13 case dismissed before confirmation is filed no later than 21
/// days after entry of the order of dismissal.
deadline dismissed-case-fee-period: 21.days after Chapter13DismissalEntered() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 2016-1(b)"

/// LBR 2016-1(b)(6)(A): if the debtor's attorney withdraws, the fee
/// application is filed no later than 21 days after legal representation is
/// discontinued.
deadline discontinued-representation-fee-period: 21.days after RepresentationDiscontinued() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 2016-1(b)"

/// LBR 2071-1: within 7 days of its first meeting, unless the United States
/// trustee has filed it, an official committee files a report naming its
/// chairperson and service designee.
deadline committee-report-period: 7.days after CommitteeFirstMeeting() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 2071-1"

/// LBR 2090-2: an attorney ordered to show cause why discipline should not
/// be imposed responds within 30 days after service of the order.
deadline show-cause-period: 30.days after ShowCauseOrderServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 2090-2"

/// LBR 2090-2(d)(4): an attorney objecting to the chief district judge's
/// interim disciplinary order files the objection and memorandum with the
/// clerk of the district court within 14 days of its entry.
deadline interim-discipline-objection-period: 14.days after InterimDisciplineOrderEntered() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 2090-2(d)"

/// LBR 2091-1(c): unless the court orders otherwise, an attorney may not
/// withdraw within 21 days before a trial or hearing on any matter.
deadline attorney-withdrawal-period: 21.days before TrialOrHearingScheduled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 2091-1(c)"

/// LBR 3007-1(a), (c): the claimant files and serves a response to an
/// objection to its claim not later than 30 days after service of the
/// objection.
deadline claim-objection-response-period: 30.days after ClaimObjectionServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 3007-1(c)"

/// LBR 3012-1(b): an objection to confirmation based on the value of
/// personal property subject to a lien, or to the failure to list it as
/// secured, is filed and served within 14 days after the § 341 meeting is
/// concluded.
deadline valuation-objection-period: 14.days after MeetingConcluded() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 3012-1(b)"

/// LBR 3012-1(c)(2): the creditor files and serves its appraisal within 14
/// days after the § 341 meeting of creditors.
deadline appraisal-service-period: 14.days after MeetingConcluded() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 3012-1(c)"

/// LBR 3015-2(c): an objection to a motion to modify a confirmed chapter 13
/// plan is filed and served within 21 days after its service, unless the
/// trustee notices or the court orders otherwise.
deadline modification-objection-period: 21.days after PlanModificationMotionServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 3015-2(c)"

/// LBR 3015-3(a)(1): an objection to confirmation of an initial chapter 13
/// plan is filed within 14 days after the § 341 meeting is concluded.
deadline confirmation-objection-period: 14.days after MeetingConcluded() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 3015-3(a)"

/// LBR 3016-1(b): an order granting a chapter 11 enlargement of time gives
/// creditors and parties in interest 21 days from its service to object.
deadline enlargement-objection-period: 21.days after ExclusivityEnlargementServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 3016-1(b)"

/// LBR 3020-1: unless otherwise ordered, a party presenting witnesses or
/// evidence at a chapter 11 confirmation hearing files and serves witness
/// and exhibit lists not later than 7 days before it.
deadline confirmation-witness-list-period: 7.days before ConfirmationHearingScheduled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 3020-1"

/// LBR 4001-1(a)(8): a request for a preliminary hearing on a motion for
/// relief from stay is filed no later than 7 days after entry of the order
/// setting the final hearing or service of the motion.
deadline preliminary-stay-hearing-period: 7.days after StayHearingOrderEntered() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 4001-1(a)"

/// LBR 4002-1(b): payment advices for the 60 days before the petition are
/// not filed but provided to the trustee and the United States trustee at
/// least 7 days before the first date set for the § 341 meeting.
deadline payment-advices-meeting-period: 7.days before FirstMeetingDate() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 4002-1(b)"

/// LBR 4002-1(b): and not later than 45 days after the petition is filed.
deadline payment-advices-outer-period: 45.days after PetitionFiled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 4002-1(b)"

/// LBR 4002-1(d): a chapter 13 debtor eligible for a discharge files LBR
/// Form 4002-1 within 21 days after the trustee's Certification of Final
/// Payment, or the case may close without a discharge.
deadline discharge-certification-period: 21.days after FinalPaymentCertified() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 4002-1(d)"

/// LBR 4002-1(f)(1): absent a written extension, within 21 days after
/// service of a trustee's written request the debtor serves the information
/// or documents or moves for a protective order.
deadline trustee-request-period: 21.days after TrusteeRequestServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 4002-1(f)"

/// LBR 5011-1(b): a response to a motion for withdrawal of the reference is
/// filed with the bankruptcy court within 14 days from service of the
/// motion.
deadline withdrawal-response-period: 14.days after WithdrawalMotionServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 5011-1(b)"

/// LBR 5011-1(c): a reply memorandum may be filed within 7 days after
/// service of the response.
deadline withdrawal-reply-period: 7.days after WithdrawalResponseServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 5011-1(c)"

/// LBR 6004-1(a)(1)(F): a written objection to a noticed use, sale or
/// lease, with a request for hearing, is filed and served not later than 21
/// days from service of the notice unless the court shortens it.
deadline sale-objection-period: 21.days after SaleNoticeServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 6004-1(a)"

/// LBR 6004-1(a)(2)(A): unless otherwise ordered, within 21 days after a
/// sale outside the ordinary course and before disbursing proceeds, the
/// trustee or debtor in possession files a report of sale.
deadline sale-report-period: 21.days after SaleCompleted() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 6004-1(a)"

/// LBR 6007-1(a): an objection to a noticed abandonment is filed and served
/// within 14 days of service of the notice, or the property is deemed
/// abandoned.
deadline abandonment-objection-period: 14.days after AbandonmentNoticeServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 6007-1(a)"

/// LBR 6007-1(c)(1): a trustee who finds the property burdensome or of
/// inconsequential value executes and returns a notice of abandonment
/// within 14 days of receiving the request.
deadline abandonment-request-response-period: 14.days after AbandonmentRequestReceived() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 6007-1(c)"

/// LBR 7016-1(a): each party files and serves its Preliminary Pretrial
/// Statement within 30 days of entry of the Order Governing Pretrial and
/// Trial Procedures or other deadline the court sets.
deadline pretrial-statement-period: 30.days after PretrialOrderEntered() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 7016-1(a)"

/// LBR 7026-1: opposition to a motion for a protective order or to compel
/// discovery is filed within 7 days of the motion's filing.
deadline discovery-opposition-period: 7.days after DiscoveryMotionFiled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 7026-1"

/// LBR 7026-1: a reply memorandum is filed within 7 days of the filing of
/// the memorandum in opposition.
deadline discovery-reply-period: 7.days after DiscoveryOppositionFiled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 7026-1"

/// LBR 9011-2(a): an individual appearing pro se files and serves notice of
/// a change of mailing address or telephone number within 14 days from the
/// change.
deadline pro-se-address-period: 14.days after ProSeAddressChanged() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 9011-2(a)"

/// LBR 9013-1(a)-(b): unless the court orders otherwise, a response
/// memorandum opposing a motion or application is filed within 21 days from
/// service on the certificate of service, the period of the 21-day notice.
deadline motion-response-period: 21.days after MotionServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 9013-1(b)"

/// LBR 9013-1(c): a reply memorandum may be filed within 7 days after
/// service of the response memorandum.
deadline motion-reply-period: 7.days after ResponseServed() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 9013-1(c)"

/// LBR 9070-1: a party contesting the authenticity or accuracy of the
/// standing trustee's financial records files and serves its witnesses,
/// exhibits and reasons at least 7 days before the hearing.
deadline trustee-records-challenge-period: 7.days before TrusteeRecordsHearingScheduled() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 9070-1"

/// LBR 9072-1(e): if no response is filed in time, the movant submits a
/// proposed order within 7 days of the expiration of the response period.
deadline unopposed-order-period: 7.days after ResponseTimeExpired() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 9072-1(e)"

/// LBR 9072-1(f): unless otherwise ordered, within 7 days after a hearing
/// or trial the prevailing party submits a proposed order conforming to the
/// decision.
deadline post-hearing-order-period: 7.days after HearingOrTrialHeld() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 9072-1(f)"

/// LBR 9072-1(g): unless otherwise ordered, within 7 days of informing the
/// court of a resolution before hearing or trial, the party seeking relief
/// submits a proposed order conforming to it.
deadline agreed-order-period: 7.days after ResolutionReported() counted_by frbp9006 cite "S.D. Ohio LBR 9072-1(g)"
